# Firebase Realtime Database Plan

## 1. Firebase Database

The SkillsTrack Learner Support Portal will use **Firebase Realtime Database** to store application data. Firebase will allow the application to store, retrieve, update and delete learner information and application records.

The database will contain the following main areas:

```text
users/
    {uid}/
        displayName
        email
        role
        createdAt

tasks/
    {taskId}/
        userId
        title
        category
        dueDate
        priority
        completed
        createdAt

bookings/
    {bookingId}/
        userId
        topic
        preferredDate
        notes
        status

scores/
    {scoreId}/
        userId
        score
        duration
        completedAt

resources/
    {resourceId}/
        title
        type
        url
        description
```

This structure is based on the suggested Firebase structure in the project brief.

---

## 2. Users

The `users` section stores basic information about registered users.

Example:

```text
users/
    abc123/
        displayName: "Lerato"
        email: "lerato@example.com"
        role: "learner"
        createdAt: "2026-08-31T10:00:00"
```

The `{uid}` represents the authenticated Firebase user's unique ID.

The user's password will NOT be stored in the database. Passwords must be handled by Firebase Authentication.

---

## 3. Tasks

The `tasks` section stores learner learning tasks.

Example:

```text
tasks/
    task001/
        userId: "abc123"
        title: "Complete JavaScript exercise"
        category: "JavaScript"
        dueDate: "2026-09-05"
        priority: "High"
        completed: false
        createdAt: "2026-08-31T10:30:00"
```

The `userId` connects the task to the learner who created it.

This allows the application to display the correct learner's tasks and calculate completed, outstanding and overdue work.

---

## 4. Support Bookings

The `bookings` section stores support-session requests.

Example:

```text
bookings/
    booking001/
        userId: "abc123"
        topic: "JavaScript Functions"
        preferredDate: "2026-09-03"
        notes: "I need help understanding functions."
        status: "pending"
```

The booking starts with a status such as `pending`. An assessor or administrator can update the booking status where that functionality is included in the approved scope.

---

## 5. Game Scores

The `scores` section stores results from the mini-game or quiz.

Example:

```text
scores/
    score001/
        userId: "abc123"
        score: 80
        duration: 45
        completedAt: "2026-09-10T12:00:00"
```

The `userId` identifies which learner achieved the score.

---

## 6. Learning Resources

The optional `resources` section stores learning resources.

Example:

```text
resources/
    resource001/
        title: "JavaScript Functions"
        type: "article"
        url: "https://example.com/javascript-functions"
        description: "Introduction to JavaScript functions."
```

