# REST API Plan

The application will use the Firebase Realtime Database REST API to communicate with Firebase.

## GET — Read Data

GET will be used to retrieve data from Firebase.

Example:

```text
GET /tasks.json
```

Purpose:

* Retrieve learner tasks.
* Display tasks on the dashboard.
* Calculate progress.
* Search and filter task information.

---

## POST — Create Data

POST will be used when a new record needs to be created.

Example:

```text
POST /tasks.json
```

Purpose:

* Create a new learning task.
* Firebase generates a unique task ID.

---

## PUT — Replace Data

PUT will be used when an existing Firebase record needs to be completely replaced.

Example:

```text
PUT /tasks/{taskId}.json
```

Purpose:

* Replace all information belonging to a specific task.

---

## PATCH — Update Data

PATCH will be used to change selected fields without replacing the entire record.

Example:

```text
PATCH /tasks/{taskId}.json
```

Purpose:

* Change the task's completion status.
* Change the priority.
* Change the due date.

For example:

```json
{
    "completed": true
}
```

---

## DELETE — Delete Data

DELETE will be used to remove a task.

Example:

```text
DELETE /tasks/{taskId}.json
```

Before deleting a task, the application will show a confirmation dialog so that the user does not accidentally delete important information.

---

# Firebase Security Plan

The database must not allow unrestricted public write access. Users should only access information appropriate to their authenticated identity and role.

The application will use the authenticated user's Firebase UID to identify ownership.

For example:

```text
tasks/
    task001/
        userId: "abc123"
```

If the authenticated user has UID `abc123`, the application can determine that the task belongs to that user.

Security rules will be configured so that unauthenticated users cannot write learner data and users cannot access another learner's private task information.

---

# Firebase CRUD Plan

| Operation | Firebase method | Application use         |
| --------- | --------------- | ----------------------- |
| Create    | POST            | Add a new task          |
| Read      | GET             | Display tasks           |
| Update    | PUT/PATCH       | Edit or complete a task |
| Delete    | DELETE          | Remove a task           |

The project requires documented REST CRUD operations and, in Month 2, evidence of POST, GET, PUT/PATCH, DELETE and verification through GET or an equivalent method.

